---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Terms — FastShared"
  description="The rules for using FastShared. Ephemeral by design, no accounts, and what you can and cannot upload."
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="frame pt-16 pb-24 max-w-[760px]">
    <h1
      class="font-display font-bold text-milk mb-8"
      style="font-size: clamp(44px, 7vw, 96px); line-height: 0.95; letter-spacing: -0.04em;"
    >
      Terms.
    </h1>

    <p class="font-mono text-[12px] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-amber mb-10">
      Effective 19 April 2026 · v1.0
    </p>

    <div class="space-y-7 text-milk/75 text-[17px] leading-[1.7]">
      <p>
        These are the terms for using FastShared — the iOS, iPadOS, and
        macOS app, the <code class="font-mono text-[14px] text-amber">fastsha.red</code>
        website, the <code class="font-mono text-[14px] text-amber">fsh.re</code>
        short-link service, and any related APIs (collectively, "the
        Service"). The Service is operated by Matheus Kindrazki, an
        individual developer based in Brazil. In this document, "we", "us",
        and "our" refer to that operator, and "you" refers to the person
        using the Service.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-milk text-[26px] md:text-[30px] pt-6" style="letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
        Acceptance
      </h2>
      <p>
        By installing, opening, or using the Service you agree to these
        terms. If you do not agree, do not use the Service. These terms apply
        alongside our
        <a href="/privacy" class="text-amber hover:underline">Privacy policy</a>
        and any platform-specific rules (App Store, TestFlight) that govern
        how Apple distributes the app to you.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-milk text-[26px] md:text-[30px] pt-6" style="letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
        What the Service does
      </h2>
      <p>
        FastShared is an ephemeral file-sharing utility. You pick a file. You
        pick how long the link should live, within a configurable window
        between 5 minutes and 30 days. The Service stores the file in a
        private bucket and returns a short URL you can paste anywhere. At
        the end of the window the URL stops working; shortly after, the
        file is deleted.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Service does not offer permanent hosting. There is no "keep
        forever" option. If you need a copy of a file, keep your own copy.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-milk text-[26px] md:text-[30px] pt-6" style="letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
        Your account — there isn't one
      </h2>
      <p>
        FastShared does not use accounts. Instead, your device mints a
        private token on first launch and uses it to authenticate with our
        API. The token lives in your device's Keychain. Anyone with access
        to your unlocked device can use FastShared as you. You can revoke
        the token by deleting the app (from the perspective of the client)
        or by emailing
        <a href="mailto:support@fastsha.red" class="text-amber hover:underline">support@fastsha.red</a>
        and asking us to invalidate the associated device row.
      </p>
      <p>
        The recipient of a FastShared link also does not sign in. The link
        is the credential. Treat it accordingly — do not post it somewhere
        you would not want the file to be downloaded from.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-milk text-[26px] md:text-[30px] pt-6" style="letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
        What you can upload
      </h2>
      <p>
        You can upload any file you have the right to share. You keep
        ownership of everything you upload. By uploading, you grant us the
        narrow, time-bounded permission to store the file, generate a link
        to it, and serve downloads until the link expires, and to delete it
        when the window closes. That's it.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-milk text-[26px] md:text-[30px] pt-6" style="letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
        What you cannot upload
      </h2>
      <p>
        You may not use the Service to upload, share, or distribute:
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-3 pl-1">
        <li class="flex gap-3 items-start">
          <span class="text-amber flex-none" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          <span>Child sexual abuse material (CSAM). We report it to
          authorities and delete the file immediately.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3 items-start">
          <span class="text-amber flex-none" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          <span>Malware, viruses, ransomware, or anything designed to harm
          a recipient's device.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3 items-start">
          <span class="text-amber flex-none" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          <span>Content that infringes someone else's copyright, trademark,
          or other intellectual property rights.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3 items-start">
          <span class="text-amber flex-none" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          <span>Non-consensual intimate imagery, doxxing material,
          harassment, or content intended to threaten or intimidate a
          specific person.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3 items-start">
          <span class="text-amber flex-none" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          <span>Content that is illegal in Brazil (where the Service is
          operated) or in your jurisdiction.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-3 items-start">
          <span class="text-amber flex-none" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          <span>Content used to phish, defraud, or impersonate another
          person or organisation.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If we become aware that your upload falls into any of these
        categories — through a report at
        <code class="font-mono text-[14px] text-amber">/report/:token</code>,
        through a law-enforcement request, or through our own review — we
        will revoke the link immediately and delete the file. We may also
        delete your device's token so the same installation cannot continue
        to use the Service.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-milk text-[26px] md:text-[30px] pt-6" style="letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
        Rate limits and abuse
      </h2>
      <p>
        The Service applies rate limits per device, per IP, and per token,
        to keep it responsive for everyone. Current limits are published in
        our
        <a href="https://github.com/MatheusKindrazki/fastshared/blob/main/docs/architecture/security.md" class="text-amber hover:underline">architecture documentation</a>
        and may change without notice. When you hit a limit, the API
        responds with HTTP 429 and a
        <code class="font-mono text-[14px] text-amber">Retry-After</code>
        header. Attempting to circumvent rate limits, or using multiple
        devices to amplify a single actor's usage, is a breach of these
        terms.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-milk text-[26px] md:text-[30px] pt-6" style="letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
        No permanent storage
      </h2>
      <p>
        Every upload is ephemeral. When the link expires it returns
        <code class="font-mono text-[14px] text-amber">410 Gone</code>, and
        the underlying object is deleted automatically within hours. There
        is no soft-delete, no grace period you can appeal to, and no way to
        recover a file after deletion. If a file matters to you, you must
        keep your own copy.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-milk text-[26px] md:text-[30px] pt-6" style="letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
        Service availability
      </h2>
      <p>
        We operate the Service with reasonable care but do not guarantee
        uninterrupted availability. The Service may be slow, rate-limited,
        or temporarily unavailable for maintenance, outages at our
        sub-processors (principally Cloudflare and Neon), or other reasons
        outside our control. We may discontinue the Service, temporarily or
        permanently, on reasonable notice — typically 30 days — or without
        notice in an emergency.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-milk text-[26px] md:text-[30px] pt-6" style="letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
        "As is" — no warranty
      </h2>
      <p>
        The Service is provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis,
        without warranties of any kind, whether express, implied, statutory,
        or otherwise, including without limitation warranties of
        merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, non-infringement,
        or that the Service will be uninterrupted or error-free. You use
        the Service at your own risk.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-milk text-[26px] md:text-[30px] pt-6" style="letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
        Limitation of liability
      </h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, we shall not be
        liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential,
        exemplary, or punitive damages arising from your use of the Service,
        including loss of profits, goodwill, data, or other intangible
        losses. Our total cumulative liability for any direct damages shall
        not exceed the greater of (a) the amount you have paid us in the 12
        months preceding the event giving rise to the claim, or (b) fifty
        Brazilian reais (BRL 50,00). Some jurisdictions do not allow these
        limitations; in such jurisdictions our liability is limited to the
        smallest extent permitted by law.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-milk text-[26px] md:text-[30px] pt-6" style="letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
        Indemnity
      </h2>
      <p>
        You agree to indemnify and hold us harmless against any claim or
        damages arising from content you upload or from your breach of
        these terms. This is a standard provision; we do not invoke it for
        ordinary use.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-milk text-[26px] md:text-[30px] pt-6" style="letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
        Changes to these terms
      </h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms. Material changes will be announced inside
        the app and dated at the top of this page. Continued use of the
        Service after a change takes effect means you accept the revised
        terms. If you disagree with a change, stop using the Service; your
        uploaded files will continue to expire and delete on their original
        schedule.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-milk text-[26px] md:text-[30px] pt-6" style="letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
        Governing law
      </h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the Federative Republic of
        Brazil. Any dispute that cannot be resolved informally will be
        submitted to the courts of the City of Curitiba, State of Paraná,
        Brazil, unless mandatory consumer-protection law in your
        jurisdiction grants you the right to sue in your local courts.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-milk text-[26px] md:text-[30px] pt-6" style="letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
        Contact
      </h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms:
        <a href="mailto:support@fastsha.red" class="text-amber hover:underline">support@fastsha.red</a>.
        Abuse reports for a specific link: use the in-app Report action, or
        the unauthenticated
        <code class="font-mono text-[14px] text-amber">POST /v1/report/:token</code>
        endpoint.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
